[0.007, "o", "\u001b[1mOuterwear & Coats, Jeans, and Sweaters generated $1.05M combined, driving 31.4% of total net revenue\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1mover the last 12 months.\u001b[0m                                                                            \r\n\r\n\u001b[36m                                                                                                    \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m \u001b[0m\u001b[1m                  \u001b[0m\u001b[36m \u001b[0m\u001b[1m            \u001b[0m\u001b[36m \u001b[0m\u001b[36mShare of Total \u001b[0m\u001b[1m   \u001b[0m\u001b[1m \u001b[0m\u001b[36m \u001b[0m\u001b[1m           \u001b[0m\u001b[36m \u001b[0m\u001b[1m               \u001b[0m\u001b[36m \u001b[0m\u001b[1m                  \u001b[0m\u001b[36m \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m \u001b[0m\u001b[36mCategory\u001b[0m\u001b[1m         \u001b[0m\u001b[1m \u001b[0m\u001b[36m \u001b[0m\u001b[36mNet Revenue\u001b[0m\u001b[1m \u001b[0m\u001b[36m \u001b[0m\u001b[36mRevenue\u001b[0m\u001b[1m           \u001b[0m\u001b[1m \u001b[0m\u001b[36m \u001b[0m\u001b[36mItems Sold\u001b[0m\u001b[1m \u001b[0m\u001b[36m \u001b[0m\u001b[36mAvg Item Price\u001b[0m\u001b[1m \u001b[0m\u001b[36m \u001b[0m\u001b[36mYoY Revenue Growth\u001b[0m\u001b[36m \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"]
[0.000, "o", "────────────────────────────────────── \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m \u001b[0m\u001b[1mOuterwear & Coats\u001b[0m \u001b[36m \u001b[0m$415,978.39 \u001b[36m \u001b[0m12.48%             \u001b[36m \u001b[0m2,872      \u001b[36m \u001b[0m$144.84        \u001b[36m \u001b[0m+97.7%            \u001b[36m \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m \u001b[0m\u001b[1mJeans\u001b[0m             \u001b[36m \u001b[0m$373,226.69 \u001b[36m \u001b[0m11.19%             \u001b[36m \u001b[0m3,795      \u001b[36m \u001b[0m$98.35         \u001b[36m \u001b[0m+97.6%            \u001b[36m \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m \u001b[0m\u001b[1mSweaters\u001b[0m          \u001b[36m \u001b[0m$259,170.03 \u001b[36m \u001b[0m7.77%              \u001b[36m \u001b[0m3,474      \u001b[36m \u001b[0m$74.60         \u001b[36m \u001b[0m+95.7%            \u001b[36m \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m                                                                                                    \u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[3m(Note: Net revenue excludes cancelled and returned items across the trailing 365 days.)\u001b[0m             \r\n\r\n\u001b[1m • \u001b[0m\u001b[1mOuterwear leads on ticket size:\u001b[0m Outerwear & Coats holds the #1 spot despite 923 fewer units sold \r\n\u001b[1m   \u001b[0mthan Jeans, powered by a hig"]
[0.000, "o", "h average ticket price of $144.84 vs. Jeans at $98.35.               \r\n\u001b[1m • \u001b[0m\u001b[1mJeans drives volume and stability:\u001b[0m Jeans is our largest volume driver among premium categories   \r\n\u001b[1m   \u001b[0m(3,795 items across 3,675 orders), maintaining nearly identical YoY growth (+97.6%) to Outerwear \r\n\u001b[1m   \u001b[0m(+97.7%).                                                                                        \r\n\u001b[1m • \u001b[0m\u001b[1mCold-weather apparel dominates the top tiers:\u001b[0m Combined, these three categories account for nearly\r\n\u001b[1m   \u001b[0ma third of all sales; preserve depth of stock in Outerwear sizing early in Q3 to prevent         \r\n\u001b[1m   \u001b[0mstockouts at peak demand.                                                                        \r\n"]
