[0.000, "o", "  \u001b[0m(55.7% margin) versus $46.41 (46.5% margin) for Jeans; this $33.12 premium per unit allows       \r\n\u001b[1m   \u001b[0mOuterwear to generate significantly higher bottom-line profit despite 1,062 fewer units sold.    \r\n\u001b[1m • \u001b[0m\u001b[1mJeans incurs higher post-purchase friction:\u001b[0m Jeans suffers from a higher return rate (10.51% vs.  \r\n\u001b[1m   \u001b[0m9.40%), concentrated particularly in the Men's department (11.48%), diluting Jeans' volume       \r\n\u001b[1m   \u001b[0madvantage with additional reverse-logistics loss.                                                \r\n\u001b[1m • \u001b[0m\u001b[1mMerchandising recommendation:\u001b[0m Prioritize feature placement and campaign budget toward Outerwear  \r\n\u001b[1m   \u001b[0mheading into peak season to maximize cash contribution per order, while auditing Men's Jeans     \r\n\u001b[1m   \u001b[0msizing guides to lower returns.                                                                  \r\n"]
