[0.006, "o", "\u001b[1mOur return rate spiked to 10.38% in July 2026 (+72 bps above the trailing 3-month average of 9.66%),\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[1mdriven predominantly by double-digit return rates in Jeans and Dresses.\u001b[0m                             \r\n\r\n\u001b[36m                                                                                                    \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m \u001b[0m\u001b[1m                  \u001b[0m\u001b[36m \u001b[0m\u001b[1m                    \u001b[0m\u001b[36m \u001b[0m\u001b[1m               \u001b[0m\u001b[36m \u001b[0m\u001b[1m            \u001b[0m\u001b[36m \u001b[0m\u001b[36mBaseline Comparison (Trailing\u001b[0m\u001b[36m \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m \u001b[0m\u001b[36mMonth\u001b[0m\u001b[1m            \u001b[0m\u001b[1m \u001b[0m\u001b[36m \u001b[0m\u001b[36mTotal Items Ordered\u001b[0m\u001b[1m \u001b[0m\u001b[36m \u001b[0m\u001b[36mReturned Items\u001b[0m\u001b[1m \u001b[0m\u001b[36m \u001b[0m\u001b[36mReturn Rate\u001b[0m\u001b[1m \u001b[0m\u001b[36m \u001b[0m\u001b[36m3M Avg)\u001b[0m\u001b[1m                      \u001b[0m\u001b[36m \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"]
[0.000, "o", "─────────────────── \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m \u001b[0m\u001b[1mJuly 2026 (Spike)\u001b[0m \u001b[36m \u001b[0m\u001b[1m7,585\u001b[0m               \u001b[36m \u001b[0m\u001b[1m787\u001b[0m            \u001b[36m \u001b[0m\u001b[1m10.38%\u001b[0m      \u001b[36m \u001b[0m\u001b[1m+0.72 pts vs. 9.66% Baseline\u001b[0m \u001b[36m \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m \u001b[0mAugust 2026       \u001b[36m \u001b[0m8,945               \u001b[36m \u001b[0m864            \u001b[36m \u001b[0m9.66%       \u001b[36m \u001b[0mNormal baseline              \u001b[36m \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m \u001b[0mJune 2026         \u001b[36m \u001b[0m6,542               \u001b[36m \u001b[0m658            \u001b[36m \u001b[0m10.06%      \u001b[36m \u001b[0m+0.40 pts                    \u001b[36m \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m \u001b[0mMay 2026          \u001b[36m \u001b[0m6,280               \u001b[36m \u001b[0m613            \u001b[36m \u001b[0m9.76%       \u001b[36m \u001b[0m+0.10 pts                    \u001b[36m \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m \u001b[0mApril 2026        \u001b[36m \u001b[0m5,633               \u001b[36m \u001b[0m538            \u001b[36m \u001b[0m9.55%       \u001b[36m \u001b[0m-0.11 pts                    \u001b[36m \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[36m                                                                                                    \u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[3m(Note: Baseline is calcul"]
[0.000, "o", "ated across the trailing 3-month window April–June 2026 at 9.66%. \u001b[0m         \r\n\u001b[3mIncomplete current month excluded.)\u001b[0m                                                                 \r\n\r\n\u001b[1m • \u001b[0m\u001b[1mJeans and Dresses drove the aggregate spike:\u001b[0m In July, the return rate for Jeans jumped to 13.29% \r\n\u001b[1m   \u001b[0m(+3.31 pts above its baseline of 9.98%), producing 17 excess returned items; Dresses spiked to   \r\n\u001b[1m   \u001b[0m13.08% (+5.13 pts above its baseline of 7.95%), producing 12 excess returns.                     \r\n\u001b[1m • \u001b[0m\u001b[1mConcentrated brand outliers:\u001b[0m The surge within these categories was driven by specific high-return\r\n\u001b[1m   \u001b[0mlabels—notably Allegra K in Dresses (24.24% return rate across 33 orders) and Calvin Klein Jeans \r\n\u001b[1m   \u001b[0m(45.45% return rate across 11 orders).                                                           \r\n\u001b[1m • \u001b[0m\u001b[1mCorrective next step:\u001b[0m The QA and Merchandising team should review customer return reason codes   \r\n\u001b[1m   \u001b[0mand sizing chart"]
[0.000, "o", "s for Allegra K dresses and Calvin Klein Jeans to eliminate fit discrepancies    \r\n\u001b[1m   \u001b[0mbefore placing Q4 reorders.                                                                      \r\n"]
